FADE IN:

INT. HARBOURMASTER'S OFFICE - MORNING

Charts pinned three deep on every wall. A kettle shrieks.

ODILE VANCE, 50's, the harbourmaster, sharp-eyed, speaks with a clipped Northern Highland accent.

ODILE
Nobody sails until that lamp is lit.

CONSTABLE
The fishermen won't like it.

ODILE
The fishermen can like it from the dock.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE STEPS - DAY #1#

Wind tears at the railings. Mara climbs behind Wick, two steps at a time.

MARA
How many steps?

WICK
Two hundred and nine. I count them every morning.

INT. LAMP ROOM - CONTINUOUS

The great lens sits cold and dusty. A smear of soot across the glass.

WICK
Somebody's been up here.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Somebody had.

INT./EXT. FERRY - DUSK #2#

The little ferry chugs across the harbour mouth, lantern swinging.

FERRYMAN
I saw a light on the rocks last night. Green, like a bottle.

ODILE
And you said nothing?

FERRYMAN
You never asked.

/*
EXT. ROCKS - NIGHT

Cut: the green light, seen up close.
*/

EXT. QUAYSIDE - NIGHT

Pip runs down the quay, out of breath.

PIP
Constable! There's a boat with no lights!

CONSTABLE
Where?

EST. HARBOUR TOWN - NIGHT #2A#

Every window dark but one.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And in that one window, someone was counting coins.

INT. CONSTABLE'S COTTAGE - NIGHT #3#

Mara sits across the table, the ledger between them.

MARA
It was never short. Someone was paying for silence.

CONSTABLE
Then we find out whose.

> FADE OUT.
